{"id":305,"name":"lairon","speciesId":305,"dex":305,"form":"normal","generation":3,"types":["steel","rock"],"stats":{"hp":60,"attack":90,"defense":140,"special-attack":50,"special-defense":50,"speed":40},"abilities":[{"name":"sturdy","hidden":false},{"name":"rock-head","hidden":false},{"name":"heavy-metal","hidden":true}],"height":9,"weight":1200,"baseExp":151,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/305.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/305.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/305.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/305.ogg","genus":"Iron Armor Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"ruby","text":"LAIRON tempers its steel body by drinking highly nutritious mineral springwater until it is bloated. This POKéMON makes its nest close to springs of delicious water."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"LAIRON feeds on iron contained in rocks and water. It makes its nest on mountains where iron ore is buried. As a result, the POKéMON often clashes with humans mining the iron ore."},{"version":"emerald","text":"When two LAIRON meet in the wild, they fight for territory by bashing into each other with their steel bodies. The sound of their collision carries for miles."},{"version":"firered","text":"It habitually shows off its strength with the size of sparks it creates by ramming its steel body into boulders."},{"version":"diamond","text":"For food, it digs up iron ore. It smashes its steely body against others to fight over territory."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"It loves iron ore. Groups of them fight for territory by bashing one another with their steel bodies."},{"version":"black-2","text":"Lairon fight over territory, and when their steel bodies collide, sparks fly."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Lairon tempers its steel b